<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I116fdd5d1891d7d9a5c45f047a59e78a94142c23" commit="5b33a9439425ec7a7ece7334b5882fc8f66c1ae3" commit_message="CHROMIUM: i2c: tegra: Add arbitration lost support  Add support for issuing a bus clear when arbitration lost occurs. Some generations have hardware support for this, and for those generations, use it. For older generations that don't have hardware support, use the supplied GPIOs and the i2c bus clear algorithm to do the bus clear.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46922 TEST=built and booted, suspend/resume cyles  Change-Id: I116fdd5d1891d7d9a5c45f047a59e78a94142c23 Signed-off-by: Rhyland Klein &lt;rklein@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317411 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317411" owner_email="rklein@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/11/317411/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I517bd170bc650b9312918190c7d9832d35de944f" commit="244aa6f0392fdb17330c6d8695924ff4736fc2ef" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: tegra210: fix property names for i2c  Fix the property names from scl-gpio and sda-gpio to 'nvidia,' prefixed versions which the driver expects.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46922 TEST=built and booted, suspend/resume cyles  Change-Id: I517bd170bc650b9312918190c7d9832d35de944f Signed-off-by: Rhyland Klein &lt;rklein@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317412 Reviewed-by: Jimmy Zhang &lt;jimmzhang@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317412" owner_email="rklein@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/12/317412/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Iea79160d68680b0c55ba49761b3f5d0f71937b03" commit="8b2083f02eb32a0c179e00a09dc9c2050f1089f7" commit_message="CHROMIUM: i2c: tegra: Enable MULTI_MASTER_MODE  Optionally enable multi-master mode in I2C_CNFG reg based on hw features. Using single/multi-master mode bit introduced for Tegra210, whereas multi-master mode is enabled by default in HW for T124 and earlier Tegra SOC. Enabling this bit doesn't explicitly start treating the bus has having multiple masters, but will start checking for arbitration lost and reporting when it occurs.  The Tegra210 I2C controller supports single/multi master mode. Add chipdata for Tegra210 and its compatibility string so that Tegra210 will select data that enables multi master mode correctly.  Add &quot;nvidia,multimaster-mode&quot; property to enable multimaster specific prerequisites:  1. Enable 1st level clock always set.  2. Disable 2nd level clock gating (slcg which   is supported from T124 SOC and later chips)  This DT property should be added to the DT node for any bus which actively has multiple masters present.  Signed-off-by: Shardar Shariff Md &lt;smohammed@nvidia.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46922 TEST=built and booted, suspend/resume cyles  Change-Id: Iea79160d68680b0c55ba49761b3f5d0f71937b03 Signed-off-by: Rhyland Klein &lt;rklein@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321152 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321152" owner_email="rklein@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/52/321152/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Iab040e915c3971d8eac2487beb24508a6a028474" commit="c888157e860b2ee4bcc19e51a745ec6c7dc9aa41" commit_message="CHROMIUM: i2c: tegra: add multimaster mode property to binding  Document the usage &quot;nvidia,multimaster-mode&quot; property  Signed-off-by: Shardar Shariff Md &lt;smohammed@nvidia.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46922 TEST=built and booted, suspend/resume cyles  Change-Id: Iab040e915c3971d8eac2487beb24508a6a028474 Signed-off-by: Rhyland Klein &lt;rklein@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321154 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321154" owner_email="rklein@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/54/321154/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I27beeb7783e609338e5cc8c2695206db189de51c" commit="e158c9128c4618cb8854d8791787b7f9d4a1877e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: i2c: tegra: fix issue observed in error cases  To summarize the issue:  In SW: For i2c message transfer, packet header and data payload is posted and then required error/packet completion interrupts are enabled later.  In HW flow: HW process the packet just after packet header is posted, if ARB lost/NACK error occurs (SW will not handle when error happens as error interrupts are not enabled at this point) HW assumes error is acknowledged and  clears current data in FIFO, But SW here posts the remaining data payload which still stays in FIFO as stale data (data without packet header).  Now once the interrupts are enabled, SW handles ARB lost/NACK error by clearing the ARB lost/NACK interrupt. Now HW assumes that SW attended the error and will parse/process stale data(data without packet header) present in FIFO which causes invalid NACK errors.  Fix: Enable the error interrupts before posting the packet into FIFO which make sure HW to not clear the fifo and disable the packet mode before acknowledging errors (ARB lost/NACK error) to not process any stale data.  As error interrupts are enabled before posting the packet header to avoid preempting.  Signed-off-by: Shardar Shariff Md &lt;smohammed@nvidia.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46922 TEST=built and booted, suspend/resume cyles  Change-Id: I27beeb7783e609338e5cc8c2695206db189de51c Signed-off-by: Rhyland Klein &lt;rklein@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321155 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321155" owner_email="rklein@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="11" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/55/321155/11" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Id930036254ae145af1734fb80f03ddffd561f23e" commit="e96c9da6b4e11c58aa860f8a69a152b3f7ffe21a" commit_message="CHROMIUM: i2c: tegra: Adjust RX FIFO Trigger for Tegra210  On Tegra210 platforms, change the RX trigger level to assert after 4 words are full in the FIFO. This will help reduce the number of interrupts generated.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46922 TEST=built and booted, suspend/resume cyles  Change-Id: Id930036254ae145af1734fb80f03ddffd561f23e Signed-off-by: Rhyland Klein &lt;rklein@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321156 Reviewed-by: Jimmy Zhang &lt;jimmzhang@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321156" owner_email="rklein@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/56/321156/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I246ee7918976c377d0bf915d1403a8a889b916b9" commit="7badf3feb10b5e20dcef780eaebfa9ca08443ac3" commit_message="CHROMIUM: i2c: tegra: Add cl_dvfs clock enabling for PWR_I2C  Added cl_dvfs clocks enabling for PWR_I2C in i2c driver.  Based on work by Chaitanya Bandi.  BUG=None TEST=booted and verified cl dvfs clks held  Change-Id: I246ee7918976c377d0bf915d1403a8a889b916b9 Signed-off-by: Rhyland Klein &lt;rklein@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321660 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321660" owner_email="rklein@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/60/321660/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="If557d28fe42f8d0520dcdfa28e504f965659bc77" commit="df94f610a7aec2badfbf96dc4d5b20830f0e4e78" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: tegra210: Add CL DVFS clks to PWR I2C  PWR I2C needs to have CLDVFS REF and SOC clks enabled, add them to the I2C5 DT node so they can be references from the driver.  BUG=None TEST=Booted, verified clocks enabled  Change-Id: If557d28fe42f8d0520dcdfa28e504f965659bc77 Signed-off-by: Rhyland Klein &lt;rklein@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321661 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321661" owner_email="rklein@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="11" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/61/321661/11" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ib9006ace0da52bb196bf936326082566d3e60bfc" commit="441e378f73a1c3ed5494aabba97878033d413b15" commit_message="CHROMIUM: alt-syscall: Whitelist a couple more syscalls for Android  setns(2) is used by vold and process_vm_readv(2) is used by strace.  BUG=b:26807417,b:26832741,b:26589008 TEST=Builds for Cyan and Oak.  Change-Id: Ib9006ace0da52bb196bf936326082566d3e60bfc Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324107 Reviewed-by: Luigi Semenzato &lt;semenzato@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="324107" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/07/324107/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Iabeec78ecce07b55ca2f24a1501623228bd56711" commit="f0055868f04c9c9c62d451087f6df5008dc965ba" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iio: cros_ec: Fix potential out-of-bounds write  There are two potential issues with the sensor FIFO handling that can result in an out-of-bounds write:  - state-&gt;ring is kcalloc()'ed with the wrong element size.  It should    be sizeof(struct cros_ec_sensors_ring_sample), not sizeof(struct    ec_response_motion_sense)).  - The BUG_ON() in cros_ec_ring_handler() will not fire until after an    out-of-bounds write has occurred.  (It's also debatable as to whether    or not BUG_ON() is the appropriate way to handle this error, but    that's a separate issue.)  BUG=chromium:581751 TEST=Build and boot on Smaug.  Change-Id: Iabeec78ecce07b55ca2f24a1501623228bd56711 Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323877 Reviewed-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323877" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/77/323877/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I00b3f0434bfb8582aebad7cd0682445980b57773" commit="e466763fea549220f2e3a28ed007ae713dd98434" commit_message="common: Adds JEDEC SFDP v1.0 &amp; v1.5 encoding and decoding  Adds a header with JEDEC SFDP v1.0 (JESD216) &amp; v1.5 (JESD216A) encoding and decoding support to enable a part agnostic Serial NOR Flash driver.  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=Tested through the spi_nor driver  Change-Id: I00b3f0434bfb8582aebad7cd0682445980b57773 Signed-off-by: Ewout van Bekkum &lt;ewout@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321921 Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="321921" owner_email="ewout@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/21/321921/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><lkgm version="7872.0.0-rc4"/></manifest>